    ('provincial-flores-island-park', 'Flores Island Park', 'provincial', 49.272833, -126.165597, 'West Coast Islands', 'A large wilderness park in Clayoquot Sound, Flores Island offers coastal hiking, paddling, whale watching and beach camping. It protects old-growth Sitka spruce, salmon habitat, rocky shore, beaches and a range of coastal and marine ecosystems.', 'https://catalogue.data.gov.bc.ca/dataset/parks-ecological-reserves-and-protected-areas', 'BC Parks / DataBC — TANTALIS protected areas', '680', NULL),
