    ('provincial-gold-muchalat-park', 'Gold Muchalat Park', 'provincial', 49.866476, -126.10123, 'North Island', 'Northwest of Gold River, Gold Muchalat is an undeveloped wilderness area with opportunities for fishing, wildlife watching and rustic hiking. The park also protects winter habitat for Roosevelt elk and deer, plus salmon waters in the Muchalat River.', 'https://catalogue.data.gov.bc.ca/dataset/parks-ecological-reserves-and-protected-areas', 'BC Parks / DataBC — TANTALIS protected areas', '703', NULL),
