    ('provincial-goldstream-park', 'Goldstream Park', 'provincial', 48.475557, -123.542431, 'South Island', 'Close to Victoria, Goldstream combines old forest, waterfalls, river trails and seasonal wildflowers. In autumn, chum salmon return to spawn and draw eagles and visitors to the river; the park also has a visitor centre, picnic areas and camping.', 'https://catalogue.data.gov.bc.ca/dataset/parks-ecological-reserves-and-protected-areas', 'BC Parks / DataBC — TANTALIS protected areas', '705', NULL),
    ('provincial-gordon-bay-park', 'Gordon Bay Park', 'provincial', 48.833373, -124.201395, 'South Island', 'On the shore of Lake Cowichan, Gordon Bay is a family camping destination with a sandy swimming beach and warm summer water. The surrounding lake and valley also draw anglers, boaters and visitors interested in the area''s local history.', 'https://catalogue.data.gov.bc.ca/dataset/parks-ecological-reserves-and-protected-areas', 'BC Parks / DataBC — TANTALIS protected areas', '707', NULL),
