    ('provincial-roberts-memorial-park', 'Roberts Memorial Park', 'provincial', 49.062325, -123.774383, 'Central Island', 'A short forest trail leads to a rocky beach on Stewart Channel near Nanaimo. The park''s distinctive sandstone ledges preserve a record of ancient seabeds and provide haul-out places for sea lions.', 'https://catalogue.data.gov.bc.ca/dataset/parks-ecological-reserves-and-protected-areas', 'BC Parks / DataBC — TANTALIS protected areas', '1002', NULL),
