    ('provincial-rosewall-creek-park', 'Rosewall Creek Park', 'provincial', 49.453404, -124.781869, 'Central Island', 'A small day-use park follows Rosewall Creek through conifers and broadleaf maple south of Fanny Bay. Two picnic areas and a short riverside path make it a quiet place to watch the creek, especially in autumn.', 'https://catalogue.data.gov.bc.ca/dataset/parks-ecological-reserves-and-protected-areas', 'BC Parks / DataBC — TANTALIS protected areas', '1016', NULL),
