    ('provincial-ruckle-park', 'Ruckle Park', 'provincial', 48.780917, -123.388751, 'Gulf Islands', 'Seven kilometres of rocky shoreline, coves and bays make Ruckle a rewarding place to explore Salt Spring Island''s coast. Forest, fields and shore support abundant wildlife, while campsites overlook Swanson Channel and working farmland preserves local history.', 'https://catalogue.data.gov.bc.ca/dataset/parks-ecological-reserves-and-protected-areas', 'BC Parks / DataBC — TANTALIS protected areas', '1019', NULL),
    ('provincial-rugged-point-marine-park', 'Rugged Point Marine Park', 'provincial', 49.962827, -127.242195, 'North Island', 'Accessible only by boat, Rugged Point is a coastal stop on northern Vancouver Island''s west side. Sheltered beaches on the peninsula''s north contrast with surf-exposed outer shores, with safe anchorages for boaters in suitable conditions.', 'https://catalogue.data.gov.bc.ca/dataset/parks-ecological-reserves-and-protected-areas', 'BC Parks / DataBC — TANTALIS protected areas', '1020', NULL),
