    ('provincial-sooke-mountain-park', 'Sooke Mountain Park', 'provincial', 48.438764, -123.657325, 'South Island', 'Established near Victoria to protect wilderness, wildlife and scenic values, Sooke Mountain preserves rugged hills, lakes, forest slopes and watershed. Visitors can hike, cycle, ride horses, fish and watch wildlife in this part of the Sooke Hills greenbelt.', 'https://catalogue.data.gov.bc.ca/dataset/parks-ecological-reserves-and-protected-areas', 'BC Parks / DataBC — TANTALIS protected areas', '1103', NULL),
    ('provincial-sooke-potholes-park', 'Sooke Potholes Park', 'provincial', 48.428675, -123.711595, 'South Island', 'The Sooke River has carved deep, smooth rock pools beside this popular day-use area. The potholes formed through glacial action and swirling stones during the last ice age, creating distinctive swimming holes and river scenery.', 'https://catalogue.data.gov.bc.ca/dataset/parks-ecological-reserves-and-protected-areas', 'BC Parks / DataBC — TANTALIS protected areas', '1104', NULL),
