    ('provincial-sproat-lake-park', 'Sproat Lake Park', 'provincial', 49.292417, -124.92751, 'Central Island', 'Sproat Lake draws visitors for swimming, fishing, water skiing and windsurfing in the Alberni Valley. Short paths reach the shore and the K’ak’awin petroglyph panel, an important prehistoric carving site beside the lake.', 'https://catalogue.data.gov.bc.ca/dataset/parks-ecological-reserves-and-protected-areas', 'BC Parks / DataBC — TANTALIS protected areas', '1112', NULL),
    ('provincial-squitty-bay-park', 'Squitty Bay Park', 'provincial', 49.449242, -124.17059, 'Northern Gulf Islands', 'A small protected bay on Lasqueti Island is enclosed by rocky headlands and dry terrain. Visitors can picnic, walk out onto the point and take in distant views of Mount Baker and the Comox Glacier.', 'https://catalogue.data.gov.bc.ca/dataset/parks-ecological-reserves-and-protected-areas', 'BC Parks / DataBC — TANTALIS protected areas', '1113', NULL),
