    ('provincial-stamp-river-park', 'Stamp River Park', 'provincial', 49.342581, -124.930369, 'Central Island', 'Trails follow the Stamp River through forest and rapids to waterfalls and viewing points. Thousands of salmon gather below Stamp Falls each year before climbing the fish ladders, making the seasonal run a highlight for visitors.', 'https://catalogue.data.gov.bc.ca/dataset/parks-ecological-reserves-and-protected-areas', 'BC Parks / DataBC — TANTALIS protected areas', '1116', NULL),
